      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\), we will break it down into smaller steps and solve each part individually.\n\nFirst, let's calculate \\(23^2\\):\n\\[\n23^2 = 23 \\times 23 = 529\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate \\(2(23)(2)\\):\n\\[\n2(23)(2) = 2 \\times 23 \\times 2 = 92\n\\]\n\nThen, let's calculate \\(2^2\\):\n\\[\n2^2 = 2 \\times 2 = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we add these three results together:\n\\[\n23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2 = 529 + 92 + 4\n\\]\n\nLet's perform the addition step by step:\n\\[\n529 + 92 = 621\n\\]\n\\[\n621 + 4 = 625\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{625}\\).",
